# Joveo Button Component Guidelines

## Button Variants

### Primary Button
- Background: Primary Blue (#303F9F)
- Text: White (#FFFFFF)
- Hover: Slightly darker blue (#29358f)
- Border: None
- Shadow: Subtle elevation (shadow-xs)
- Use for: Primary actions, form submissions, main calls-to-action

```tsx
<JoveoButton variant="primary">Button</JoveoButton>
```

### Secondary Button
- Background: Light purple (#e6e8ff)
- Text: Primary Blue (#303F9F)
- Hover: Slightly darker background (#d5d7f0)
- Border: None
- Shadow: None
- Use for: Secondary actions, alternative options

```tsx
<JoveoButton variant="secondary">Button</JoveoButton>
```

### Tertiary Button
- Background: White (#FFFFFF)
- Text: Primary Blue (#303F9F)
- Hover: Very light background (#f5f5ff)
- Border: 1px solid light border color (#e2e8f0)
- Shadow: None
- Use for: Less important actions, cancel buttons

```tsx
<JoveoButton variant="tertiary">Button</JoveoButton>
```

### Text Button
- Background: Transparent
- Text: Primary Blue (#303F9F)
- Hover: Very light background (#f5f5ff)
- Border: None
- Shadow: None
- Use for: Least important actions, links within content

```tsx
<JoveoButton variant="text">Button</JoveoButton>
```

## Button Implementation

The button component should use the following class-variance-authority (cva) configuration:

```tsx
const joveoButtonVariants = cva(
  "inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&_svg]:pointer-events-none [&_svg:not([class*='size-'])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        primary: "bg-[#303F9F] text-white shadow-xs hover:bg-[#29358f]",
        secondary: "bg-[#e6e8ff] text-[#303F9F] hover:bg-[#d5d7f0]",
        tertiary: "bg-white text-[#303F9F] border border-[#e2e8f0] hover:bg-[#f5f5ff]",
        text: "bg-transparent text-[#303F9F] hover:bg-[#f5f5ff]",
        // Keep these for backwards compatibility
        default: "bg-[#303F9F] text-white shadow-xs hover:bg-[#29358f]",
        destructive: "bg-destructive text-white shadow-xs hover:bg-destructive/90",
        outline: "border bg-background shadow-xs hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground",
        ghost: "hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground",
        link: "text-[#303F9F] underline-offset-4 hover:underline",
      },
      size: {
        default: "h-9 px-4 py-2",
        sm: "h-8 rounded-md px-3 text-xs",
        lg: "h-10 rounded-md px-6",
        icon: "size-9",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "primary",
      size: "default",
    },
  }
)
```

## Usage Guidelines

1. Use the most appropriate variant based on the action's importance
2. Maintain consistent spacing between buttons (typically gap-4)
3. Align button text with Joveo typography standards
4. Use the primary button only once per form/section
5. Group related buttons together
6. Disabled state should use opacity-50
7. Always provide accessible labels for icon-only buttons
8. Buttons should be at least 36px tall for touch targets

## Responsive Design

- On mobile, increase touch targets (use size="lg")
- Consider full-width buttons on small screens
- Maintain proper spacing between buttons (min gap-3)

## Accessibility

- Ensure sufficient color contrast (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- Provide focus states for keyboard navigation
- Use aria-label for icon-only buttons
- Support screen readers with proper semantics